INSERT INTO ETFOLessonPlan VALUES('cmf43u3xu00hjvj9tfdejne9q',23,'Diwali d''hiver et autres fêtes','cmf43u3xm00h1vj9teoqunlx5',1767888000000,45,'Light exploration game: Show different types of lights (flashlight, LED candle, lantern photos). Students identify which gives light and learn ''lanternes'' as special light holders. Introduce concept of light celebrations in dark winter.','Cultural light celebration stations: 1) ''Beautiful Lanternes'' - simple paper lantern craft (12 min), 2) ''Light Traditions'' - photos and stories of different light festivals (8 min), 3) ''Winter Light Play'' - safe light exploration and shadows (7 min).','Lantern celebration circle: Students hold their completed lanterns (with LED lights) and share in darkened room. Each says one thing they learned about light celebrations. End with appreciation of all beautiful ''traditions''.','Communiquer les caractéristiques de l''hiver et leurs effets; Utiliser les phénomènes hivernaux; Développer la communication orale par des activités langagières variées','["Various safe light sources (flashlight, LED candles, lamp)","Lantern photos from different cultures","Light/dark comparison pictures","Safe lantern examples or pictures","Paper lantern craft templates (25)","Colored tissue paper and construction paper","Battery-operated tea lights for completed lanterns","Glue sticks and safety scissors (25 sets)","Cultural light festival photo collection","Simple picture books about light celebrations","Flashlights for shadow play (5-6)","White wall or sheet for shadow projections","Fun shadow-making objects","Completed student lanterns with LED lights","Darkened room capability","Circle sitting area","Cultural celebration appreciation cards"]',NULL,'Diwali d''hiver et autres fêtes','Light exploration game: Show different types of lights (flashlight, LED candle, lantern photos). Students identify which gives light and learn ''lanternes'' as special light holders. Introduce concept of light celebrations in dark winter.','Cultural light celebration stations: 1) ''Beautiful Lanternes'' - simple paper lantern craft (12 min), 2) ''Light Traditions'' - photos and stories of different light festivals (8 min), 3) ''Winter Light Play'' - safe light exploration and shadows (7 min).','Lantern celebration circle: Students hold their completed lanterns (with LED lights) and share in darkened room. Each says one thing they learned about light celebrations. End with appreciation of all beautiful ''traditions''.','Communiquer les caractéristiques de l''hiver et leurs effets; Utiliser les phénomènes hivernaux; Développer la communication orale par des activités langagières variées',NULL,NULL,NULL,'formative','{"observable":["L''élève utilise 3 nouveaux mots français dans ses phrases","L''élève prononce clairement les sons français ciblés","L''élève comprend les instructions avec les nouveaux mots","L''élève fait les gestes associés aux mots appris"],"checkpoints":["Reconnaît les mots à l''oral sans aide visuelle","Peut répéter les mots avec la bonne prononciation","Utilise les mots en contexte approprié","Montre compréhension par actions ou réponses"]}',1,'Plan détaillé avec supports visuels',1756911653490,1757594654055,1,'fr','Français (Immersion)','{"pourDifficultés":["Focus on light recognition and simple lantern holding","Use familiar light examples (birthday candles, Christmas lights)","Simplify craft to decorating pre-made lanterns","Accept pointing and gesture responses"],"pourAvancés":["Learn names of different light celebrations","Compare different types of lanternes and lights","Help classmates with lantern crafts","Ask thoughtful questions about light traditions"],"pourLangue":["Connect to light celebrations from home cultures","Use light as universal celebration element","Allow sharing in home language about light traditions","Focus on hands-on light exploration"],"pourPEI":["Adapt lantern craft for individual motor needs","Provide sensory alternatives if light sensitivity","Use preferred participation methods","Allow flexible engagement with light activities"]}','{"vocabulary":["Diwali","lanternes","tradition"],"visualSupports":["Light source picture cards, ''lanternes'' vocabulary card with images, cultural light celebration photos","Lantern craft instruction cards, cultural light tradition pictures, shadow play safety posters, celebration appreciation vocabulary","''Traditions'' vocabulary poster, celebration appreciation phrases, lantern sharing example pictures"],"movementBreaks":["Light holding and gentle waving movements","Day/night stretching actions","Lantern craft assembly movements","Shadow play actions","Gentle light appreciation dances","Gentle lantern holding and showing movements","Light appreciation gestures"]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{"questions":["Les élèves ont-ils atteint les objectifs?","Quelles adaptations étaient nécessaires?","Que ferais-je différemment la prochaine fois?"]}',NULL,'',1,9,'core',1);
INSERT INTO ETFOLessonPlan VALUES('cmf43u3xv00hlvj9tyvfm366e',23,'Nouvel An autour du monde','cmf43u3xm00h1vj9teoqunlx5',1767974400000,45,'Calendar exploration: Show current calendar and point to ''nouvelle année'' dates. Students practice saying ''nouveau'' with new vs old object comparisons (new crayon vs used crayon). Make wishes with ''souhaits'' gestures.','New Year celebration stations: 1) ''Noise Maker Crafts'' - creating celebration shakers and horns (12 min), 2) ''New Year Around World'' - photos and cultural exploration (8 min), 3) ''Wishes and Hopes'' - drawing and sharing positive thoughts (7 min).','New Year celebration finale: Students use their noise makers for gentle ''Bonne année!'' celebration. Share one wish or happy thought. End with group countdown ''trois, deux, un... Bonne année!'' with cheering.','Exprimer le concept de nouvel an; Utiliser les phénomènes hivernaux; Développer la communication orale par des activités langagières variées','["Current year calendar","New/old object pairs for comparison","New Year celebration photos","Wish-making gesture demonstration","Paper plates, dried beans, rice for shakers","Toilet paper tubes for horns","Colorful streamers, stickers, markers","Tape and stapler (teacher use)","Global New Year celebration photo collection","World map or globe","Simple New Year traditions picture books","Drawing paper with ''My Wishes'' prompts","Crayons and colored pencils (25 sets)","Student-made noise makers","''Bonne année!'' celebration banner","Countdown number cards","Celebration space for safe movement"]',NULL,'Nouvel An autour du monde','Calendar exploration: Show current calendar and point to ''nouvelle année'' dates. Students practice saying ''nouveau'' with new vs old object comparisons (new crayon vs used crayon). Make wishes with ''souhaits'' gestures.','New Year celebration stations: 1) ''Noise Maker Crafts'' - creating celebration shakers and horns (12 min), 2) ''New Year Around World'' - photos and cultural exploration (8 min), 3) ''Wishes and Hopes'' - drawing and sharing positive thoughts (7 min).','New Year celebration finale: Students use their noise makers for gentle ''Bonne année!'' celebration. Share one wish or happy thought. End with group countdown ''trois, deux, un... Bonne année!'' with cheering.','Exprimer le concept de nouvel an; Utiliser les phénomènes hivernaux; Développer la communication orale par des activités langagières variées',NULL,NULL,NULL,'formative','{"observable":["L''élève utilise 3 nouveaux mots français dans ses phrases","L''élève prononce clairement les sons français ciblés","L''élève comprend les instructions avec les nouveaux mots","L''élève fait les gestes associés aux mots appris"],"checkpoints":["Reconnaît les mots à l''oral sans aide visuelle","Peut répéter les mots avec la bonne prononciation","Utilise les mots en contexte approprié","Montre compréhension par actions ou réponses"]}',1,'Plan détaillé avec supports visuels',1756911653491,1757594654056,1,'fr','Français (Immersion)','{"pourDifficultés":["Focus on ''new'' vs ''old'' concrete concepts","Simplify noise maker to decorating pre-made shakers","Use birthday celebrations as comparison","Accept gesture participation in countdown"],"pourAvancés":["Learn about different cultural New Year dates","Compare New Year traditions from multiple countries","Help classmates with noise maker crafts","Lead group in ''Bonne année'' celebrations"],"pourLangue":["Connect to New Year celebrations from home countries","Use New Year greetings in multiple languages","Focus on universal celebration elements","Share home culture New Year traditions"],"pourPEI":["Adapt celebration volume and intensity to individual needs","Provide alternative participation in group celebrations","Modify crafts for fine motor abilities","Use preferred celebration elements"]}','{"vocabulary":["nouveau","année","souhaits"],"visualSupports":["''Nouvelle année'' calendar visual, ''nouveau/vieux'' comparison poster, ''souhaits'' gesture cards with pictures","Noise maker craft instruction cards, world New Year celebration map, wish-making picture prompts, cultural celebration photos with simple explanations","''Bonne année!'' greeting poster, countdown visual support, celebration gesture cards"],"movementBreaks":["New vs old movement comparisons","Wish-making star-reaching gestures","Noise maker testing and gentle celebration dancing","Wish-making movements and gestures","Cultural celebration movements from photos","Noise maker celebration movements","Group countdown actions","Gentle New Year cheering"]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{"questions":["Les élèves ont-ils atteint les objectifs?","Quelles adaptations étaient nécessaires?","Que ferais-je différemment la prochaine fois?"]}',NULL,'',1,10,'core',1);
INSERT INTO ETFOLessonPlan VALUES('cmf43u3xw00hnvj9tfhw56nq2',23,'Cuisine d''hiver réconfortante','cmf43u3xm00h1vj9teoqunlx5',1768233600000,45,'Warm and cold food sorting: Present pictures of foods and drinks. Students sort into ''chaud'' (warm/hot) and ''froid'' (cold) categories. Introduce winter comfort foods that warm us up, focusing on ''soupe'' as warm food.','Winter comfort food stations: 1) ''Soupe Kitchen'' - pretend soup making with safe materials (10 min), 2) ''Chocolat Chaud'' - hot chocolate sensory exploration (8 min), 3) ''Biscuits and Treats'' - winter treat sorting and pretend baking (9 min).','Comfort food sharing circle: Students choose favorite winter comfort food picture and share ''J''aime la soupe'' or ''J''aime le chocolat.'' Group responds ''Mmm, c''est bon!'' End with gratitude for warm, delicious food.','Décrire les caractéristiques de l''hiver et leurs effets; Utiliser les phénomènes hivernaux; Développer la communication orale par des activités langagières variées','["Food picture cards (mix of hot and cold foods)","Two sorting baskets labeled ''chaud'' and ''froid''","Real examples: warm soup picture, ice cream picture","Temperature gesture cards","Play kitchen setup with pots, spoons, ladles","Colored water for ''soup'' (safe)","Soup ingredient pictures and play vegetables","Hot chocolate powder for safe smelling","Warm cups with cocoa scent (safe)","Marshmallow props (real or foam)","Cookie cutters and play dough","Biscuit and treat picture collection","Cultural winter food photos","3 station setup areas with clear boundaries","Individual comfort food picture cards","Response phrase cards ''Mmm, c''est bon!''","Circle sitting area","Gratitude gesture cards"]',NULL,'Cuisine d''hiver réconfortante','Warm and cold food sorting: Present pictures of foods and drinks. Students sort into ''chaud'' (warm/hot) and ''froid'' (cold) categories. Introduce winter comfort foods that warm us up, focusing on ''soupe'' as warm food.','Winter comfort food stations: 1) ''Soupe Kitchen'' - pretend soup making with safe materials (10 min), 2) ''Chocolat Chaud'' - hot chocolate sensory exploration (8 min), 3) ''Biscuits and Treats'' - winter treat sorting and pretend baking (9 min).','Comfort food sharing circle: Students choose favorite winter comfort food picture and share ''J''aime la soupe'' or ''J''aime le chocolat.'' Group responds ''Mmm, c''est bon!'' End with gratitude for warm, delicious food.','Décrire les caractéristiques de l''hiver et leurs effets; Utiliser les phénomènes hivernaux; Développer la communication orale par des activités langagières variées',NULL,NULL,NULL,'formative','{"observable":["L''élève utilise 3 nouveaux mots français dans ses phrases","L''élève prononce clairement les sons français ciblés","L''élève comprend les instructions avec les nouveaux mots","L''élève fait les gestes associés aux mots appris"],"checkpoints":["Reconnaît les mots à l''oral sans aide visuelle","Peut répéter les mots avec la bonne prononciation","Utilise les mots en contexte approprié","Montre compréhension par actions ou réponses"]}',1,'Plan détaillé avec supports visuels',1756911653492,1757594654057,1,'fr','Français (Immersion)','{"pourDifficultés":["Focus on familiar comfort foods (soup, hot chocolate)","Use real food examples and pictures","Simplify to hot/cold sorting activity","Accept pointing to preferred foods"],"pourAvancés":["Learn additional winter food vocabulary (pain, fromage)","Discuss cooking processes and ingredients","Help classmates with food vocabulary","Compare comfort foods from different cultures"],"pourLangue":["Connect to comfort foods from home cultures","Use food pictures as universal language","Allow sharing food names in home language","Focus on sensory food experiences"],"pourPEI":["Adapt for food allergies and sensitivities","Provide alternative sensory experiences if needed","Use preferred food examples","Allow observational participation in food activities"]}','{"vocabulary":["soupe","chocolat","biscuits"],"visualSupports":["Hot/cold food sorting chart, ''soupe'' vocabulary card with steaming bowl, temperature gesture reference poster","Soup making instruction picture cards, hot chocolate vocabulary poster, biscuit types chart, cultural comfort food photos","''J''aime...'' sentence starter poster, comfort food appreciation cards, gratitude and thankfulness visual supports"],"movementBreaks":["Hot food blowing gestures","Cold food shivering movements","Soup stirring motions","Soup stirring and ladling actions","Hot chocolate sipping motions","Cookie mixing and rolling movements","Food appreciation gestures","Gentle gratitude movements"]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{"questions":["Les élèves ont-ils atteint les objectifs?","Quelles adaptations étaient nécessaires?","Que ferais-je différemment la prochaine fois?"]}',NULL,'',1,11,'core',1);
INSERT INTO ETFOLessonPlan VALUES('cmf43u3xw00hpvj9trw3g50pe',23,'Musique et chansons d''hiver','cmf43u3xm00h1vj9teoqunlx5',1768320000000,45,'Musical instrument exploration: Present various instruments (bells, shakers, drums). Students identify which make ''musique'' and practice gentle playing. Introduce ''chanson'' by humming familiar tune and having students guess.','Winter music exploration stations: 1) ''Chanson Learning'' - simple French winter songs with actions (10 min), 2) ''Cultural Music'' - listening and moving to winter celebration music (8 min), 3) ''Dance and Movement'' - winter celebration dancing (9 min).','Winter music concert: Students choose their favorite song or music from the lesson and perform for the group (humming, dancing, or playing instruments). Audience responds with gentle applause and appreciation.','Lire les sons et leur correspondance; Chanter la discrimination auditive des sons; Développer la communication orale par les activités musicales','["Simple musical instruments: bells, shakers, small drums","Musical instrument picture cards","Audio clips of familiar tunes for guessing","Speaker or device for music","French winter song sheets with pictures","Audio recordings of simple French winter songs","Cultural winter music collection (Christmas, Hanukkah, etc.)","Movement scarves and ribbons (25)","Simple rhythm instruments for each student","Cultural dance photos and video examples","Large open space for dancing","Music player with volume control","Student choice of instruments or scarves","Performance area setup","Audience appreciation cards","Music from lesson for background support"]',NULL,'Musique et chansons d''hiver','Musical instrument exploration: Present various instruments (bells, shakers, drums). Students identify which make ''musique'' and practice gentle playing. Introduce ''chanson'' by humming familiar tune and having students guess.','Winter music exploration stations: 1) ''Chanson Learning'' - simple French winter songs with actions (10 min), 2) ''Cultural Music'' - listening and moving to winter celebration music (8 min), 3) ''Dance and Movement'' - winter celebration dancing (9 min).','Winter music concert: Students choose their favorite song or music from the lesson and perform for the group (humming, dancing, or playing instruments). Audience responds with gentle applause and appreciation.','Lire les sons et leur correspondance; Chanter la discrimination auditive des sons; Développer la communication orale par les activités musicales',NULL,NULL,NULL,'formative','{"observable":["L''élève utilise 3 nouveaux mots français dans ses phrases","L''élève prononce clairement les sons français ciblés","L''élève comprend les instructions avec les nouveaux mots","L''élève fait les gestes associés aux mots appris"],"checkpoints":["Reconnaît les mots à l''oral sans aide visuelle","Peut répéter les mots avec la bonne prononciation","Utilise les mots en contexte approprié","Montre compréhension par actions ou réponses"]}',1,'Plan détaillé avec supports visuels',1756911653493,1757594654058,1,'fr','Français (Immersion)','{"pourDifficultés":["Focus on listening and simple movements","Use familiar tune patterns with French words","Provide visual song supports with lots of pictures","Accept any form of musical participation"],"pourAvancés":["Learn complete verses of French winter songs","Help teach songs to classmates","Create original winter song verses","Lead group musical activities"],"pourLangue":["Connect to musical traditions from home cultures","Use music as universal language","Allow singing in home language mixed with French","Focus on rhythm and movement over lyrics"],"pourPEI":["Adapt for sensory sensitivities to music volume/types","Provide alternative ways to participate in musical activities","Use preferred musical elements or instruments","Allow quiet participation or observation"]}','{"vocabulary":["chanson","musique","danser"],"visualSupports":["Musical instrument identification