INSERT INTO ETFOLessonPlan VALUES('cmf43u4ct01drvj9tjrzd6kih',23,'Découvrir les sons autour de nous','cmf43u4cs01dpvj9t3z11w2yu',1765814400000,45,'Sound mystery walk - students close eyes and listen while teacher makes familiar classroom sounds (pencil sharpener, door closing, water pouring)','Sound exploration stations - students rotate through listening activities identifying animal sounds, musical sounds, and nature sounds','Sound scavenger hunt - students share one new sound they discovered and demonstrate how to make it safely','Explorer les sons et leur correspondance; Expérimenter avec la discrimination auditive des sons; Développer la démarche scientifique par l''investigation scientifique','["various classroom objects that make distinct sounds (class set of 25-30)","quiet background music (class set of 25-30)","audio recordings of different sound categories (class set of 25-30)","headphones or speakers (class set of 25-30)","sound identification cards with pictures (class set of 25-30)","étiquettes autocollantes (2 planches)","tampons motivants avec encreur (5 tampons)","certificats d''encouragement (30 copies)"]',NULL,'Découvrir les sons autour de nous','Sound mystery walk - students close eyes and listen while teacher makes familiar classroom sounds (pencil sharpener, door closing, water pouring)','Sound exploration stations - students rotate through listening activities identifying animal sounds, musical sounds, and nature sounds','Sound scavenger hunt - students share one new sound they discovered and demonstrate how to make it safely','Explorer les sons et leur correspondance; Expérimenter avec la discrimination auditive des sons; Développer la démarche scientifique par l''investigation scientifique',NULL,NULL,NULL,'formative','{"observable":["L''élève identifie 3 sources de sons différents dans l''environnement","L''élève décrit les sons avec des mots: fort/faible, aigu/grave","L''élève fait vibrer des objets pour créer des sons","L''élève explique: ''Le son vient des vibrations''"],"checkpoints":["Distingue entre sons naturels et sons fabriqués","Utilise le vocabulaire scientifique: vibration, son, bruit","Prédit quels objets feront des sons forts/faibles","Fait des liens entre vibrations et production de sons"]}',1,'Plan détaillé avec supports visuels',1756911654029,1757594654703,1,'fr','Sciences de la nature','{"pourDifficultés":["Provide picture cards alongside all sounds for visual support","Start with very obvious, contrasting sounds (door slam vs whisper)","Allow students to keep eyes open during listening activities","Use hand gestures and body movements to reinforce sound concepts"],"pourAvancés":["Challenge students to identify sound sources without visual clues","Introduce sound sequencing games (remember 3-4 sounds in order)","Have students create their own sound mysteries for classmates","Explore sound direction (where is the sound coming from?)"],"pourLangue":["Pre-teach key vocabulary (son, entendre, écouter) with visual supports","Use bilingual picture cards showing sound sources","Pair French sound words with English cognates where possible","Provide sound identification cards with both languages"],"pourPEI":["Modify seating for optimal hearing conditions","Use vibrating speakers or tactile sound experiences for hearing impaired students","Provide noise-reducing headphones if overwhelmed by sounds","Allow extra processing time for sound identification responses"]}','{"vocabulary":["son","entendre","écouter"],"visualSupports":["ear symbol poster, ''listening detective'' badge for each student","picture cards matching sounds, sound wave demonstration with ribbon"],"movementBreaks":["Répéter des comptines avec gestes : ''Tête, épaules, genoux et pieds'' (2 minutes)","Former des lettres dans l''air avec nos doigts : A, B, C (3 minutes)","Faire une pause lecture : s''étirer comme un chat qui se réveille (2 minutes)","Étirer nos doigts et mains d''écrivains : ouvrir, fermer, tourner (2 minutes)","Étirer notre dos d''écrivains : rotation douce des épaules (2 minutes)","Ranger nos idées : faire semblant de mettre nos pensées dans une boîte (2 minutes)"]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{"questions":["Les élèves ont-ils atteint les objectifs?","Quelles adaptations étaient nécessaires?","Que ferais-je différemment la prochaine fois?"]}',NULL,'',3,1,'core',1);
INSERT INTO ETFOLessonPlan VALUES('cmf43u4cu01dtvj9t4rhs937y',23,'Sons forts et sons doux','cmf43u4cs01dpvj9t3z11w2yu',1765900800000,45,'Volume control demonstration - teacher uses voice and simple instruments to show loud and soft, students copy with hand gestures (big gestures for loud, tiny for soft)','Loud and soft exploration with everyday objects - students experiment making loud and soft sounds with paper, blocks, and containers','Volume matching game - students listen to sounds and show with body movements whether sounds are loud or soft','Découvrir les sons et leur correspondance; Expérimenter avec la discrimination auditive des sons; Développer la démarche scientifique par l''investigation scientifique','["simple instruments like shakers or drums (class set of 25-30)","volume control poster","paper sheets (class set of 25-30)","wooden blocks (class set of 25-30)","plastic containers (6-8 needed for group work)","cotton balls (class set of 25-30)","recording sheets (class set of 25-30)","lingettes pour nettoyer les mains (1 paquet)","chemises individuelles (30 chemises)","boîte de rangement pour travaux (1 grande boîte)"]',NULL,'Sons forts et sons doux','Volume control demonstration - teacher uses voice and simple instruments to show loud and soft, students copy with hand gestures (big gestures for loud, tiny for soft)','Loud and soft exploration with everyday objects - students experiment making loud and soft sounds with paper, blocks, and containers','Volume matching game - students listen to sounds and show with body movements whether sounds are loud or soft','Découvrir les sons et leur correspondance; Expérimenter avec la discrimination auditive des sons; Développer la démarche scientifique par l''investigation scientifique',NULL,NULL,NULL,'formative','{"observable":["L''élève identifie 3 sources de sons différents dans l''environnement","L''élève décrit les sons avec des mots: fort/faible, aigu/grave","L''élève fait vibrer des objets pour créer des sons","L''élève explique: ''Le son vient des vibrations''"],"checkpoints":["Distingue entre sons naturels et sons fabriqués","Utilise le vocabulaire scientifique: vibration, son, bruit","Prédit quels objets feront des sons forts/faibles","Fait des liens entre vibrations et production de sons"]}',1,'Plan détaillé avec supports visuels',1756911654030,1757594654704,1,'fr','Sciences de la nature','{"pourDifficultés":["Provide visual supports alongside all sound activities","Use exaggerated sound contrasts (very loud vs very quiet)","Allow tactile exploration of vibrating objects","Offer picture cards for sound vocabulary"],"pourAvancés":["Challenge students to create complex sound patterns","Introduce sound analysis and comparison activities","Have students teach sound concepts to younger students","Explore scientific explanations for sound phenomena"],"pourLangue":["Pre-teach key sound vocabulary with visual and audio supports","Use bilingual sound identification materials","Connect French sound words to home language equivalents","Provide sound vocabulary cards with pictures and translations"],"pourPEI":["Modify volume levels based on individual sensitivities","Use vibrating objects for tactile sound experience","Provide alternative communication methods for responses","Allow extra processing time for sound identification"]}','{"vocabulary":["fort","doux","volume"],"visualSupports":["volume meter drawing with big and small sections, hand gesture reference chart","loud/soft comparison chart with pictures, volume gesture reminders"],"movementBreaks":["Faire l''alphabet avec notre corps : A comme arbre (étirer les bras), B comme ballon (forme ronde) (3 minutes)","Imiter les animaux des histoires : sauter comme un lapin, voler comme un oiseau (3 minutes)","Danser avec les sons : ''a'' avec les bras, ''o'' en rond, ''i'' pointu (3 minutes)","Étirer nos doigts et mains d''écrivains : ouvrir, fermer, tourner (2 minutes)","Faire une révérence à nos nouvelles connaissances (1 minute)","Célébrer nos apprentissages : applaudir, lever les bras, sourire (2 minutes)"]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{"questions":["Les élèves ont-ils atteint les objectifs?","Quelles adaptations étaient nécessaires?","Que ferais-je différemment la prochaine fois?"]}',NULL,'',3,2,'core',1);
